#3604
A Sandy Shore~
   In the distance to your north and south, you see towering black cliffs that
form a small lagoon to the east. The cliffs provide shelter from the raging
waters, and have allowed the formation of this sandy inlet. Pale water surges
onto the shore after each breaking wave, leaving white film behind at the
contour of its reach. The sand is opaque, which in turn absorbs the heat from
the sun, making your feet noticeably warmer. To your west is a thick, topical
jungle.
~
