#3605
A Sandy Shore~
   Black cliffs rise out of the sand to the north, and curve out to the east
like a demon's horn. The tide swells inland, then quickly rolls back into the
small lagoon to the east. A tropical jungle outlines the beach to your west
that, upon further notice, appears to have been trimmed somewhat. Slash marks
cover the palms, and whole bushels of various plant life have been mutilated,
allowing a crude passage.
