#3606
A Sandy Shore~
   To your east, a calm lagoon has been formed by the island's cradling rock
formation, and outstretched at the shore of the lagoon is a small black-sand
beach. West of here, outlining the beach, is a thick tropical jungle. Glancing
further west, you can see the cliffs circle around the fringes of the jungle
in the form of a circle. From this observation, you realize that the only way
into the heart of the isle is through the small opening into the lagoon.
