#3607
A Sandy Shore~
   Dark cliffs hang over the cove to the south and curl to the east, forming
a small lagoon. The cliffs prevent any significant ocean activity, allowed the
formation of this small, sandy inlet. After walking about for a bit, you
notice your footprints on the sand's surface, and while doing so become aware
of others - others that, when observed closely, look to be fresly made.
However, these prints are not your own. The prints recede into a lush jungle
to your west.
